    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the r1 gate and that 009 and 020 are merged; read the two REST handlers and CompleteDecisionTool.</step>
    <step order="2">Write the two tools; add the ledger rows.</step>
    <step order="3">Write the contract and must-not-leak tests; run them, the MCP suites, ArchTests and the conformance host.</step>
    <step order="4">Measure the publish-size delta; record it in the PR.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="6">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the REST search route applies its access trim inside the endpoint (not a reusable service call), STOP and escalate before copying it (spec MUST NOT copy authorization).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md rows "Document search" and "Record search": ISemanticSearchService + IRetrievalAccessTrim (PublicContracts) and IRecordSearchService back the REST routes; CAPABILITY-INDEX rows for semantic search and record search.</existing>
    <extension>The services are reused unchanged; the tools are the extension (thin MCP adapters on r1's host), as spec "Placement &amp; New Components" states.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>With the legacy agent removed, Copilot users cannot search Spaarke documents or records (FR-02 fails).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build; dotnet test (contract/Api/Mcp, auth/Mcp, ArchTests, Mcp.Conformance.Host)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Search/SearchDocumentsTool.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Search/FindRecordsTool.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/Search/SearchToolsContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/Search/SearchToolsMustNotLeakTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">For the same caller and query, each tool's hit ids and order equal the REST route's.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (must-not-leak): a document the access trim removes for the caller never appears in either tool's content or structuredContent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no HttpContext or an unauthenticated one returns isError UserContextRequired and calls no service.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">At 50 hits the serialised result is under 64 KiB; model-visible text has no field outside the slim row list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">McpToolAuthorization.ValidateTool passes; ArchTests and the conformance host pass with both tools registered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-02, FR-15, NFR-02, NFR-05, NFR-07. uac-r2 reviews the caller-path diff.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
